From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:25:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/etnaviv: turn the core clocks off on remove

When the etnaviv-gpu driver is unbound after the master has been
unbound, as at rmmod, the driver core resumes the device before
remove() and drops its reference with pm_runtime_put_sync(). etnaviv
uses autosuspend with a 200 ms delay, so the put only arms the
autosuspend timer. etnaviv_gpu_platform_remove() then disables runtime
PM, which cancels the timer, and etnaviv_gpu_rpm_suspend() never runs:
the driver core then marks the device suspended without calling it.
The clock enable done by etnaviv_gpu_rpm_resume() is never undone, and
the enable count survives the driver in the clock framework. The same
holds whenever user space keeps the device active, for example through
power/control, also when only the GPU is unbound.

Make remove() leave the hardware in a defined state whatever references
are held: resume the GPU explicitly, disable runtime PM, turn its
clocks off and mark it suspended, then undo the autosuspend setting
from probe. Without CONFIG_PM, bind and unbind enable and disable the
clocks, so remove() leaves them alone.

etnaviv_gpu_hw_suspend() is not called: it could write to the command
buffer, which the component unbind has already freed.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on the Allwinner A733 NPU, the enable counts
of the reg, bus and core clocks stay unchanged over three rounds each of
rmmod and insmod, unbind and bind of the GPU alone, and rmmod and insmod
with power/control set to "on"; without the fix they go up by one per
rmmod round.

Fixes: a8c21a5451d8 ("drm/etnaviv: add initial etnaviv DRM driver")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c
index c4375859dfe9..b09f91bbfc56 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c
@@ -1992,7 +1992,21 @@ static void etnaviv_gpu_platform_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct etnaviv_gpu *gpu = dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev);
 
 	component_del(&pdev->dev, &gpu_ops);
-	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
+	/*
+	 * Leave the hardware in a defined state: resume the core and, with
+	 * runtime PM disabled, disable its clocks here, as no suspend
+	 * callback runs after this point. Without runtime PM, bind and
+	 * unbind handle the clocks.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PM) && !pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev)) {
+		pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
+		etnaviv_gpu_clk_disable(gpu);
+		pm_runtime_set_suspended(&pdev->dev);
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pdev->dev);
+	} else {
+		pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
+	}
+	pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 
 	mutex_destroy(&gpu->lock);
 	mutex_destroy(&gpu->sched_lock);
